 "notes": "Three parallel claims after gelation: mechanics (h10), encapsulation viability (h11), RGDS adhesion (h14); mechanics and viability both hang off h8 and meet at h16, adhesion is the second branch (h13->h14). Mechanical data are text-only (no figure). h9 network density is argued (no mesh measurement). h13 incorporation of RGDS is not verified in the packet (basis argued). All cell data are in vitro vs a design variable -> PRP biological. Figures opened: F1, F3, F4, F5. Packet anomaly: F3 image file shows paper Fig. 4 (CMFDA + phase contrast) while its caption concatenates Fig. 3 (EDAC reaction) and Fig. 4. r5->h15 rules_out: RGES ~ unmodified shows spreading is sequence-specific, not a peptide/charge artefact. r2 is the multimodal node: viable fraction = fluorescent count in one channel registered to total count in the phase-contrast view of the same field.",
 "migrated_from": "r04/graphs/Biomaterials__s0142-9612(02)00177-1.json"
